PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The consensus overwhelmingly identifies "Strawberry Fields Forever" as the primary Beatles song that opens with a chord jump from the tonic to the minor fifth chord ($I \to v$). While tracks such as "She's Leaving Home" and "Any Time at All" also exhibit this harmonic movement, "Strawberry Fields Forever" remains the most prominent and widely documented example in musicological literature. Erroneous candidates like "Yesterday," "Penny Lane," and "A Hard Day's Night" have been evaluated and ruled out based on their chord progressions.
}

